## Facade interface
- `BookingServiceFacade`: added `void changeDeadline(String trackingId, Date arrivalDeadline)`, keeping the boundary types (`String`, `java.util.Date`) consistent with the rest of the interface — no `TrackingId`, `Cargo`, or command DTO leaks into presentation code.

## Facade implementation
- `DefaultBookingServiceFacade`: implements `changeDeadline` by converting the identifier and delegating once to the application service, mirroring the style of `changeDestination`:

```java
@Override
public void changeDeadline(String trackingId, Date arrivalDeadline) {
    bookingService.changeDeadline(
            new TrackingId(trackingId),
            arrivalDeadline);
}
```

No repository lookups, domain mutation, or date parsing happen in the facade — that ownership stays with the task-1 application service.

## Test
- Added `DefaultBookingServiceFacadeTest`, a container-free JUnit test using a hand-written `BookingService` spy (no mocking framework) asserting: the tracking-id string converts to an equivalent `TrackingId`, the same `Date` instance reaches the service, and delegation happens exactly once.

